<title>USA: U.S. Senate rejects plan to index capital gains.</title>
<headline>U.S. Senate rejects plan to index capital gains.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1997-06-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Senate rejected an amendment to index capital gains for inflation before final passage of its tax-cut package Friday.</p>
<p>Senate Finance Committee Chairman William Roth, a Delaware Republican, said while he would like to provide greater tax relief, indexing capital gains for inflation was a proposal that President Clinton strongly opposed.</p>
</text>
